  "_citation_audit": "2026-07-26 link-integrity audit: this file's 21 wells (2023-2025 readings) have NO working public citation to their source Year Books. Both source_index_urls were 404 and the 2024-25 source_url pointed at the 2017-18 edition. Index url replaced with the live cgwbpnm root; the two editions remain OPEN TRACES. CGWB documents ARE retrievable at cgwb.gov.in/cgwbpnm/public/uploads/documents/<opaque-id>file.pdf, but there is no listing page that enumerates Year Books, which is why this family is still the highest-value unwatched source.",
  "_citation_trace_2026_07_26": "The TN 2024-25 edition (publication id 2023, posted 25 Mar 2026) is therefore unretrievable today; these 21 wells keep their 2023-24/2024-25 labels with no working public citation. RETRIEVAL IS BROKEN AT CGWB'S END - established 2026-07-26, do not repeat this. The publications warehouse at cgwb.gov.in/cgwbpnm/ LISTS both 2024-25 Year Books with titles, posting dates and publication ids, but there is no working public route to the PDFs. Eight automated routes were tried and all return the same 33 KB Drupal 404 ('paged nahin mila', plain openresty HTTP/2 404 - no WAF, no captcha, no challenge): download/<id>; publication-detail/<id>; the CSRF POST to publication/<id> followed by the download, replicating the site's own downloadPdf() JS; a cookie-jar session; deriving the path from the thumbnail id; a directory listing on uploads/documents/; search engines (not indexed); and the retired /Regions/<REGION>/Reports/ path. CONFIRMED IN A REAL BROWSER by the maintainer the same day: the page renders and the publications are visible, but the download does not work there either. So this is NOT a bot block, NOT a session problem and NOT something a browser fetch solves - an earlier version of this note said 'fetch it from a browser session', which was wrong. Only /cgwbpnm/ itself and /cgwbpnm/public/* static assets serve; every other route under /cgwbpnm/ 404s, which looks like a reverse-proxy misconfiguration on their side. The id scheme is <unix-seconds><random>, verified three ways (1688105823 = 30 Jun 2023 matches the 2017-18 PDF's own creation timestamp; 1774431953 and 1774326882 match the two 2026 posting dates), but the thumbnail and the PDF get DIFFERENT random suffixes, so the path cannot be derived from anything the listing exposes. NEXT STEPS, in order: (1) the cgwb-yearbook-* registry entries watch the download/<id> link set, so a re-upload or a route fix changes the set and we get told; (2) failing that, email CGWB SECR Chennai / CR Nagpur, or RTI. Not an engineering problem."
